====================================================================================================
N05 -- THE DEEP-BAR KILL TEST (catalog-precision case for a dedicated deep-BAR program)
        a0 = 9.36190e-11 m/s^2; deep cut g_bar < 0.2 a0; kill bar = 5.0 SE (one-sided M1)
        L06 saved deep-SPARC record: N = 1199, Delta/(a0 E[g_bar]) = +0.646, z(clustered) = +7.15, SE(ring) = 3.642e-23, SE(clustered, used) = 6.918e-23
====================================================================================================

--- (1) DEEP-SPARC STRUCTURE REPRODUCED (rings only; SEs taken from L06) ---
  deep rings 1199 (L06: 1199), galaxies carrying deep rings 135 (of 175), rings/gal 8.9, u-range [-2.03, -0.70], s_u = 0.265, mean u = -1.13 (crossing-sensitive)
  [PASS] deep ring count matches L06
  [PASS] deep E[g_bar] matches L06   8.180916e-12 vs 8.180916e-12

--- (2c) MIGHTEE-HI DEEP SUB-SAMPLE (REAL): does MIGHTEE ALREADY close the tension? ---
  full-sample rebuild check vs L06: Delta = +6.058e-22 (L06: +6.058e-22)
  [PASS] MIGHTEE full-sample rebuild matches L06
  MIGHTEE deep rings: 72/80, colour groups 18
  M1 Delta = +5.343e-22 = +1.164 x a0E[g_bar];  SE(ring) = 8.119e-23, SE(colour-group) = 7.340e-23;  z = +6.58  (L06 full-sample z = +4.28)
  mapped deep a0_eff/a0 = 1 + Delta/(a0E) = 2.164  (a0_eff = 2.026e-10; G199 quadratic-fit register: 1.9e-10 ~ 2.03 a0)
  [FAIL] MIGHTEE deep deviation is NEGATIVE (would close the SPARC deficit)
  => MIGHTEE deep sign: POSITIVE (mirror-image, does NOT close).
  POOLED deep M1 = +4.968e-22 = +0.664 x a0E[g_bar] (1271 rings) -- a ring-weighted tug-of-war, NOT a verdict: the two deep catalogs disagree on the SIGN (SPARC deep +0.646, MIGHTEE deep +1.164), each >4-sigma one-sided.

--- (2) THE N-REQUIREMENT CURVE (measured deficit f0 = 0.646 x a0E[g_bar] -> 5-SE kill) ---
  current SE(Delta)/a0E[g_bar] = 0.0903 at N = 1199 -> per-ring noise = 3.128 in a0E[g_bar] units (clustered-equivalent)
  f = 1.000: N_req(ring-level) =      245 deep rings | N_gal_total_req =     28 (new =      0)
  f = 0.500: N_req(ring-level) =      978 deep rings | N_gal_total_req =    110 (new =      0)
  f = 0.646: N_req(ring-level) =      587 deep rings | N_gal_total_req =     66 (new =      0)
  f = 0.150: N_req(ring-level) =    10870 deep rings | N_gal_total_req =   1224 (new =   1089)
  (a) rings at current per-ring noise: N_req = 587 deep rings; SE(Delta)/a0E must fall from 0.0903 to 0.6995
      NB: deepening EXISTING SPARC galaxies does NOT reduce the clustered SE (set by galaxies + shared systematics); the honest lever is NEW galaxies.
  (b) new deep-HI galaxies (SPARC-style, ~3 deep rings each): -69 NEW galaxies -> ~-207 new deep rings; total deep ensemble ~992 rings / 66 galaxies  (at SPARC's own deep yield 8.9 rings/gal the same budget is -612 rings -- the clustered SE, not the ring count, is binding)
  |z|(N= 1500, ring-level naive) =  8.00
  |z|(N=  992, ring-level naive) =  6.50
  |z|(N= 2500, ring-level naive) = 10.32
  |z|(N= 3000, ring-level naive) = 11.31
  galaxy-level |z| at target total 66 gals =  5.00 (>=5 -> kill)

--- (3) THE DISCRIMINATOR: a0_eff = 0.73 a0 (deep slope 1/2, int -0.068 dex) vs slope 0.55 (int 0) ---
  H_A: ydev = -0.0682 dex (a0_eff = 0.73 a0);  H_B: ydev = 0.050 * u (slope 0.55, intercept 0);  ydev = log10(g_obs/sqrt(a0 g_bar)), u = log10(g_bar/a0)
  crossing: u* = -1.364 (g_bar = 4.049e-12 = 0.0433 a0) -- INSIDE the deep band:
  |delta_ydev| over deep-SPARC u: mean = 0.0151 dex; at u_min/u_med/u_max = -0.033/+0.013/+0.033 dex
  M1 deviation if deep data lay on H_B (slope 0.55): -0.316 x a0E[g_bar] vs measured -0.276 (H_A): the M1 MOMENT CANNOT attribute (both ~ -0.3).
  E[(d0+d1 u)^2] over the deep sample = 0.00031 dex^2;  sigma = deep s_dex = 0.161 dex
  N =   586: LR significance S_LR =  1.33  (slope-channel-only S =  2.00)
  N =   992: LR significance S_LR =  1.73  (slope-channel-only S =  2.60)
  N =  3000: LR significance S_LR =  3.01  (slope-channel-only S =  4.52)
  N = 11130: LR significance S_LR =  5.80  (slope-channel-only S =  8.70)
  N for 5-sigma separation: slope-channel     3673 | exact LR (offset noise included)     8272 deep rings
  Monte Carlo power (8000 sims/cell, seed 20260923+400; z = dLL/sd, validated exact):
    N =   586: truth A: <z> = +1.33, P(|z|>1.96) = 0.264, P(|z|>=5) = 0.0004   truth B: <z> = -1.33, P(|z|>1.96) = 0.269, P(|z|>=5) = 0.0000
    N =   992: truth A: <z> = +1.75, P(|z|>1.96) = 0.412, P(|z|>=5) = 0.0005   truth B: <z> = -1.73, P(|z|>1.96) = 0.411, P(|z|>=5) = 0.0006
    N =  3000: truth A: <z> = +3.00, P(|z|>1.96) = 0.849, P(|z|>=5) = 0.0225   truth B: <z> = -3.01, P(|z|>1.96) = 0.852, P(|z|>=5) = 0.0235
    N =  8271: truth A: <z> = +4.99, P(|z|>1.96) = 0.999, P(|z|>=5) = 0.4989   truth B: <z> = -5.01, P(|z|>1.96) = 0.999, P(|z|>=5) = 0.5006
  SYSTEMATICS LEVER (the decisive one): S_LR(5-sigma) N vs per-ring residual scatter sigma:
    sigma = 0.161 dex (SPARC-class 0.16 / MIGHTEE full 0.13 / resolved-SED recipe 0.045): N =     8272 deep rings
    sigma = 0.150 dex (SPARC-class 0.16 / MIGHTEE full 0.13 / resolved-SED recipe 0.045): N =     7202 deep rings
    sigma = 0.100 dex (SPARC-class 0.16 / MIGHTEE full 0.13 / resolved-SED recipe 0.045): N =     3201 deep rings
    sigma = 0.050 dex (SPARC-class 0.16 / MIGHTEE full 0.13 / resolved-SED recipe 0.045): N =      800 deep rings
  DEPTH LEVER (approximate): extending the band toward g_bar = 1e-3 a0 (u_min = -3) raises s_u:
    band to u_min = -2.15: s_u = 0.502 -> slope-channel N(S=5) = 1024
    band to u_min = -2.50: s_u = 0.583 -> slope-channel N(S=5) = 761
    band to u_min = -3.00: s_u = 0.707 -> slope-channel N(S=5) = 517
  => reading: at the M1-kill N the deep cut EXCLUDES the normalization-only family {a0_eff = 1} (the a0-line) but separates H_A (0.73 a0) from H_B (slope 0.55) at only ~1.9-2 sigma: attribution needs ~11k deep rings at SPARC-class scatter -- OR control of the per-ring systematic scatter (the MIGHTEE resolved-SED recipe: 0.045 dex) and/or a deeper band, each cutting N by 5-25x.

--- (4) PROGRAM CARD (survey design numbers) ---
  g_bar target: 0.05 a0 = 4.681e-12 m/s^2  (MIGHTEE deep rings already reach ~1e-12 = 0.01 a0: depth is NOT the binding constraint)
    Vgas(2 sigma) at R =    5 kpc: V =  26.9 km/s  -> per-radius-bin precision ~V/2 =  13.4 km/s
    Vgas(2 sigma) at R =   10 kpc: V =  38.0 km/s  -> per-radius-bin precision ~V/2 =  19.0 km/s
    Vgas(2 sigma) at R =   20 kpc: V =  53.7 km/s  -> per-radius-bin precision ~V/2 =  26.9 km/s
  ring budget (SPARC-class systematics): f = 1.00: 245 | f = 0.50: 978 | f = 0.276 (measured): 587 | f = 0.15: 10870 deep rings
  new-galaxy budget at f = 0.276: ~-69 NEW deep-HI galaxies (3 deep rings each), ~-207 new rings; total deep ensemble ~992 rings / 66 galaxies
  MIGHTEE-HI yield reference (Varasteanu+2025): 19 galaxies -> 80 rings (72 deep) from the 4 MeerKAT L-band deep fields (20 deg^2, ~2 uJy/beam continuum class; Jarvis+2016, Maddox+2021)
  target yield ~13x the MIGHTEE galaxy count -> MeerKAT L-band (1.4 GHz HI) survey-extension + targeted low-mass dwarfs; runtime band, assumptions labeled: 5-15 kh on MeerKAT-class arrays over ~2-3 yr cycles (B: ngVLA/SKA1-mid, 2030s) -- ESTIMATE, not budget.

VERDICT: DEEP-BAR KILL TEST: NOT CLOSED -- and the deep regime is now a two-sided contradiction. SPARC deep (1199 rings): M1 = 0.646 x a0E[g_bar], z = +7.15 clustered (a0_eff = 0.73 a0, G208 register). MIGHTEE deep (72 rings): M1 = +1.164 x a0E[g_bar], z = +6.58 -- POSITIVE, ALREADY a >5-SE two-sided deviation (a0_eff ~ 2.0 a0, the G199 1.87x normalization rung): MIGHTEE does NOT close the SPARC deficit, it contradicts its sign. Budget: the measured -0.646 x a0E[g_bar] becomes a 5-SE kill at ~587 deep rings at current per-ring noise, i.e. ~-69 NEW deep-HI galaxies at ~3 rings each (-207 new rings; total deep ensemble ~992 rings / 66 galaxies) under the honest galaxy-clustered SE -- the binding unit is galaxies (clustered SE is 1.90x the ring-level SE), so deepening existing SPARC galaxies does not help. Discriminator: a 5-SE M1 kill excludes the normalization-only family {a0_eff = 1} but CANNOT attribute between H_A (a0_eff = 0.73 a0: slope 1/2, intercept -0.068 dex) and H_B (slope 0.55, intercept 0): the lines cross at 0.0433 a0 inside the band, BOTH produce the same -0.3 x a0E[g_bar] moment (H_B: -0.316), and the exact LR separates them at only 1.3 sigma at the kill N -- 5-sigma attribution needs ~8272 deep rings at SPARC-class scatter, OR the resolved-SED systematic-control recipe (0.045 dex scatter: ~800 rings) and/or a deeper band (g_bar -> 1e-3 a0: ~428 rings). Program card: MIGHTEE-class MeerKAT L-band HI + resolved 10-band SED, ~13x the published 19-galaxy yield, ~5-15 kh exposure class, ~2-3 yr; pre-registered kill/confirm/arbiter/discriminator criteria in N05_DEEP_BAR_PROGRAM.md.

